2. Install Jenkins on Ubuntu
Jenkins requires Java.
sudo apt update


Updates package lists.
sudo apt install fontconfig openjdk-21-jre -y


Installs Java runtime.
java -version


Checks Java installation.

Install Jenkins using the official Jenkins repository instructions for your OS version. After installation:
sudo systemctl enable jenkins


Enables Jenkins to start at boot.
sudo systemctl start jenkins


Starts Jenkins.
sudo systemctl status jenkins


Checks Jenkins status.

Jenkins normally opens at:
http://localhost:8080


Get the initial password:
sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword


